cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HYPE in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "HYPE: Hyporheic Exchange Explorer"
type: software
version: 1.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
repository-code: "https://github.com/USACE-WRISES/hype-app"
abstract: "A Windows desktop application for site-scale surface water and groundwater interaction modeling. On a model area drawn on a map it builds and runs a HEC-RAS 2025 2D surface model and a MODFLOW 6 and MODPATH 7 groundwater model, coupled one way or both ways, and a hyporheic-zone delineation, then runs solute and heat transport on the groundwater solution and produces the site reports that follow."
authors:
  - family-names: Menichino
    given-names: Garrett T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6719-6356"
    affiliation: "Environmental Laboratory, U.S. Army Engineer Research and Development Center"
keywords:
  - hyporheic exchange
  - hyporheic zone
  - groundwater
  - surface water
  - MODFLOW 6
  - MODPATH 7
  - HEC-RAS
